police in Missouri believe a man stabbed  to death on a busy highway may have been  a victim of road rage 23 year old Cody  harder was a member of the Missouri Air  National Guard he was found dead near  his vehicle in Lee's Summit Saturday  night Michelle Miller is here with the  family's search for answers Michelle  good morning good morning witnesses told  police Cody harder and another man were  in traffic when they got into an  argument Saturday police say they hope  surveillance video will help them find  the suspect  but for now Harder's family is begging  anyone with information about what  happened to him  to come forward at a press conference  Sunday Cody harder sister Kylie called  on his killer to turn himself in harder  who served a tour in Iraq was killed on  a highway in Missouri Saturday he did  not deserve Carter was found dead near  his vehicle Saturday night and what  police described as a possible road rage  incident witnesses told police they saw  harder and another man arguing on the  shoulder near where highway 291 merges  into interstate 470 they believe the  argument escalated and harder was  stabbed he stumbled and then collapsed  into traffic the suspect fled in a  vehicle going north on i-4 70 hearts  family said he owned a lawn care  business and had been driving home after  picking up a new mower in Kansas City  police released a photo of Harder's  truck a maroon 2003 Chevrolet Silverado  they're asking anyone who may have  passed by his vehicle Saturday night to  call police police are trying to put  together a description of the suspects  vehicle but said they need more  witnesses to step forward with  information Carter's mother said he was  attending classes at a local university  and only had one semester left until he  graduated with an engineering technology  degree he also leaves behind a  girlfriend he had planned to marry soon  just heartbreaking  such a tragedy unbelievable Michelle  thank you
 

